   180	## 3. Attack (ii): the covering lemma over `D - Sing D`
   181	
   182	Grok-xpoll §3.4 is right that the packet parenthetically discarded
   183	"every component of `F^{-1}(D)` is finite over `D`" and then used a consequence of
   184	it. The correct statement is *not* the discarded one (which is indeed false in
   185	general: components of `F^{-1}(D)` can and do run to the boundary over `Sing D`),
   186	and its degree is *not* `sigma`. Here is the repair, proved.
   187	
   188	Fix `p ∈ D_0`, `Delta_p` a small bidisk with `D ∩ Delta_p = {t = 0}` a disk.
   189	Since `q(B_Y) = D`, `q^{-1}(Delta_p^*) ⊆ U`, so `q^{-1}(Delta_p^*) = F^{-1}(Delta_p^*)`
   190	and this is a `d`-sheeted covering of `Delta_p^* ≃ Delta × Delta^*`.
   191	
   192	> **Lemma 3.1 (orbits = fibre points).** For `p ∈ D_0` the `H_p = <g>`-orbits on
   193	> the `d` sheets are in bijection with `q^{-1}(p)`, the orbit at `y` having size
   194	> `e_y`. Consequently the multiset `{e_y}_{y ∈ q^{-1}(p)}` **is the cycle type of
   195	> `g`**, hence is the same for every `p ∈ D_0`.
   196	> *Proof.* Shrinking `Delta_p`, `q^{-1}(Delta_p) = ⊔_{y} V_y` with `V_y` a
   197	> neighbourhood of `y`. `Y` is normal, hence analytically irreducible at `y`
   198	> (normal ⟹ unibranch), so `V_y` is connected; removing the proper analytic
   199	> subset `q^{-1}(D) ∩ V_y` keeps it connected. So `V_y \ q^{-1}(D) -> Delta_p^*`
   200	> is a **connected** covering; conservation of number for the finite flat `q`
   201	> gives its degree as `e_y`. A connected covering is one monodromy orbit.
   202	> Constancy over `D_0`: `D` irreducible and `D_0` connected make all meridians at
   203	> points of `D_0` conjugate in `pi_1(A^2 \ D)` (Zariski–van Kampen), so the cycle
   204	> type of `g` is one conjugacy invariant. ∎
   205	
   206	Lemma 3.1 already yields the *exact* conversion law that Step 2 guessed:
   207	
   208	> **Cor 3.2.** For every `p ∈ A^2`, `#F^{-1}(p) = #{y ∈ q^{-1}(p) : e_y = 1} -
   209	> #{y ∈ q^{-1}(p) ∩ B_Y : e_y = 1}`, i.e. `a_p = s_p - b_p` with
   210	> `b_p := #{y ∈ B_Y ∩ q^{-1}(p) : e_y = 1} >= 0`. In particular
   211	> **`a_p <= s_p`, with equality iff no boundary point over `p` is unramified.**
   212	
   213	So Sol-xpoll's countermodel is exactly right in kind: a monodromy-fixed sheet is
   214	a *trivial `q`-orbit*, and triviality of the orbit says nothing about which side
   215	of `B_Y` its center lies on. The packet's `#F^{-1}(p) = #Fix(H_p)` is the
   216	special case `b_p = 0`.
   217	
   218	> **Lemma 3.3 (covering lemma, repaired).** `q^{-1}(D_0) -> D_0` is an **unbranched
   219	> covering** of degree `c = #cycles(g)`; `B_Y ∩ q^{-1}(D_0)` and
   220	> `E_0 := F^{-1}(D_0)` are each unions of connected components of it. Hence

