    22	
    23	Four separate statements; each is proved below and none depends on the
    24	ledger's row bookkeeping.
    25	
    26	**(V1) Corrected identity (proved, Section 5).**  Let `S` be a smooth affine
    27	surface, `F:S->C^2` a dominant *etale* morphism of geometric degree `N`
    28	(any Keller map `C^2->C^2` is such, with `S=C^2`).  Let `B_i` be an
    29	irreducible component of the nonproper-value curve `A_F`.  Then for all `z`
    30	in a Zariski-open dense subset of `B_i`,
    31	
    32	```text
    33	N = f(z) + sum_{l in L_F, Phi(l)=closure(B_i)}  s_l * mu_l,          (2.3')
    34	```
    35	
    36	where `f(z)=#F^{-1}(z)`, `mu_l` is the generic local degree of the extended
    37	map along the dicritical `l` (the Orevkov base multiplicity), and
    38	`s_l=deg(Phi|_l : l -> closure(B_i))`.  Every other boundary place --
    39	polar/constant (image inside the target line at infinity) and
    40	finite-contracted (image a finite point) -- contributes to no generic fibre.
    41	That exclusion is *proved* (Sections 2--3), not assumed; finite-contracted
    42	boundary components do occur for general polynomial maps.
    43	
    44	**(V2) (2.3) as written is false.**  It omits the factor `s_l`.  Hand
    45	control (Section 7): `F(x,y)=(x,x^2y^4)`, `N=4`, `A_F={u=0}` irreducible, a
    46	single dicritical `l` with `mu_l=2` and `s_l=2`.  At generic `z=(0,b)` one
    47	has `f(z)=0`, so `N=4=0+s*mu=4` while `f(z)+sum mu_l=0+2=2 != 4`.  The
    48	failure mode is neither of the two anticipated in the brief: no boundary
    49	place contributes to the fibre of `z` without a dicritical image through
    50	`z`, and there is no multiplicity leakage at a special point.  The defect is
