   737	The analogous comparison lives in the *cyclic normalization* input at
   738	Section 4, equations (4.2)--(4.4); the *coordinator integration* carries it
   739	at its Section 3, equation (3.2), its Section 4 being the Euler/orbit
   740	ledger.  In both it reads, for `H=pi o f_mu` of degree `4mu`,
   741	
   742	```text
   743	4mu - 1  >=  (2mu*r + mu) + (mu - 1)  =  2mu*r + 2mu - 1,          (8.1)
   744	```
   745	with the three summands being: generic ramification-boundary mass `2mu` on
   746	each of the `r` components of `B`; the unibranch `(3,1)` cusp increment
   747	`mu`; and one unit for each of the `mu-1` deleted cyclic lines.
   748	
   749	**What `mu=1` gives.**  Term by term: `2mu*r -> 2r`, `mu -> 1`,
   750	`mu-1 -> 0`, and `4mu-1 -> 3`.  The inequality becomes `3 >= 2r+1`, hence
   751	`r=1`.  The *shape* of the argument therefore does transfer to the Keller
   752	map itself: a per-component missing-multiplicity mass of at least `2`,
   753	weighed against the budget `N-1=3`.  That is exactly the chain of
   754	Theorem 10.1 below, and it is the content the ledger's Lemma 2.3 was after.
   755	In this sense the specialization is not vacuous.
