   144	exceptional order to `-2`, and two further free blowups away from the strict
   145	line give `-1,0`.  It produces a valuation with order zero, not a Keller
   146	dicritical.  Consequently the sentence “no purely valuative or purely
   147	topological argument can close” (`R:322-328`) is **REFUTED as an impossibility
   148	claim**: the example only shows that the bare order/discrepancy condition does
   149	not close the gate; a stronger valuative theorem using Keller-specific data is
   150	not ruled out.
