   152	**Theorems 4.3 and 4.4 — CONFIRMED under H2; H3 is unused.**  For `d=3`,
   153	`a=1` leaves boundary mass two, forcing `(delta,e)=(1,2)` and `b=0`.  For
   154	`d=4`, hand partition of boundary mass `4-a` gives exactly
   155	
   156	`a=2:(1,2)`; `a=1:(1,3)`; or `a=1:(1,2)+(1,1)`.
   157	
   158	Their cycle types are respectively a transposition, a 3-cycle, and a
   159	transposition.  If `G` means the full monodromy image, irreducible `D` normally
   160	generates it by one meridian and connectedness makes it transitive.  A
   161	transitive transposition-generated subgroup on four letters is `S4`; a
   162	transitive 3-cycle-generated subgroup is `A4`.  Thus at degree four the only
